<p>
  In the equation <m>x^{3}-y^{3}=18 x y</m>, <m>y</m> is an implicitly
  function of <m>x</m> (except at <m>(0,0)</m>). The graph of
  <m>x^{3}-y^{3}=18 x y</m> is shown in <xref ref="implicitCubic"/>
</p>

<p>
  Verify that <m>(-9,9)</m>, <m>(-4,8)</m>, and <m>(-8,4)</m> are on the
  curve. Calculate the derivative of <m>y</m> implicitly. That is, find
  <m>\sdd{y}{x}</m> for the curve. Find the equations of the tangent
  lines to the curve for each of the three given points. Find the
  coordinates of any points where there is a horizontal tangent line.
  Find the coordinates of any points where there is a vertical tangent
  line. For points on the curve near the point <m>(-9,9)</m>, estimate
  the value of <m>y</m> for <m>x=-8.9</m>.
</p>
